---
Name: QtCore
Tags:
  - Name: QObject
    # True Norwegian Reference Type 🤘🏻
    SwiftImportAs: reference
    SwiftRetainOp: immortal
    SwiftReleaseOp: immortal
    SwiftSafety: unsafe

    # Note: This applies to all derived types as well,
    # and derived types should _not_ be tagged by their
    # own SwiftImportAs: reference, as that will act as
    # an upcast barrier, leaving the two types decoupled
    # in the inheritance hierarchy.

  - Name: QLibraryInfo
    Methods:
      # Marked Q_DECL_CONST_FUNCTION, which makes Swift drop the call.
      # See https://github.com/swiftlang/swift/issues/92761
      # We provide a working version() from the overlay instead
      - Name: version
        SwiftPrivate: true


  - Name: QVersionNumber
    # QList<int> * in SegmentStorage trips up the importer,
    # giving it unknown escapability, and marking it unsafe
    SwiftSafety: safe
    # FIXME: Ideally we should mark as SwiftEscapable: true
    # instead, but Swift 6.4.0 picks up the annotation for
    # forward declarations as well, resulting in errors.

  - Name: QString
    # Tripped up by QString's Data *d and char16_t *ptr
    SwiftSafety: safe
    # FIXME: Use SwiftEscapable: true for Swift > 6.4.0